     A*  test25 — command and page keys in the file-level keyword area.
     A*  They apply to every record format in the file; a record that names
     A*  the same key declares its own indicator for it and wins, matching
     A*  DDS, where a record-level keyword overrides the file-level one of
     A*  the same name.
     A*
     A*  CA12's indicator is deliberately 45, not 12.  The runtime used to
     A*  exit on ANY function key, returning the key's own number as the
     A*  indicator, so a key whose indicator equals its number could not be
     A*  told apart from that fallback — an earlier version of this test used
     A*  CA12(12) and passed with the merge disabled.  An undeclared key is
     A*  now refused (2026-11-08); 45 still keeps the two readings apart.
     A                                      CF03(03) CA12(45)
     A                                      ROLLUP(22)
     A          R INHERITS
     A                                      TEXT('Takes every file-level key')
     A            FLDA           5A  I  1  2
     A          R OVERRIDE
     A                                      TEXT('Overrides F3, adds F6')
     A                                      CF03(99) CF06(06)
     A            FLDB           5A  I  1  2
